WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.946
(playful music)

00:00:01.946 --> 00:00:06.037
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:06.037 --> 00:00:06.870
(cashier beeping)

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.850
- [Narrator] Huang Dan just
paid with a new type of money

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.788
at this pharmacy.

00:00:09.788 --> 00:00:11.550
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.855
- [Narrator] That's
because China's paper cash

00:00:12.855 --> 00:00:14.797
is going digital.

00:00:14.797 --> 00:00:18.070
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.290
- [Narrator] The digital yuan is meant

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.510
to be faster than using
credit or debit cards

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.485
on digital wallets like Apple Pay.

00:00:23.485 --> 00:00:24.510
(phone dinging)

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.300
Plus there are other incentives,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.430
like zero transaction fees for merchants

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.410
and one day, it'll even work offline.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.560
But one major difference

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.240
is that the digital yuan is 100% trackable

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.920
by China's central bank

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.520
and when it's launched nation wide,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.240
it could impact not only citizens

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.941
but also foreign companies
operating in the country.

00:00:42.941 --> 00:00:45.800
- The central bank will know who's paying,

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.750
how much they're paying,
when they're paying,

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.010
where they're paying

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:52.500
and then to analyze the
patterns of payment.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.630
- [Narrator] China's central
bank has also said it plans

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.750
to gradually replace all cash and coins

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.400
with the digital yuan.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.470
The country would be
the first major economy

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:03.440
to introduce a digital
currency in the real world.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:06.560
And while many users say the
digital yuan is easy to use,

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.943
China's money revolution could
usher in privacy concerns.

00:01:11.731 --> 00:01:15.233
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:16.066
- [Narrator] Using the phone to pay

00:01:16.066 --> 00:01:17.288
isn't a new concept for Huang

00:01:17.288 --> 00:01:21.080
since he's one of about 770
million mobile payment users

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.180
in China who rely on digital wallets

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:26.460
like Ant Group's Alipay
and Tencent's WeChat Pay.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.040
These private tech firms
hold data on transactions,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.100
which the government can access.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.070
But because the digital yuan is developed

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.230
by the central bank,

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.760
there are no third-parties

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.278
and that data sits with the government.

00:01:38.278 --> 00:01:41.790
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:44.070
- [Narrator] To begin testing
the digital currency online

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.480
and in physical stores,

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.090
last year, the Chinese central bank

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:48.720
started dolling out digital cash

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.660
through public lotteries
in cities across China.

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.160
Huang is one of the 750,000 people

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.250
who have won some piece
of the $23 million prize

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.620
in the past year.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.110
To start spending his
$30 worth of winnings,

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:04.103
Huang first downloaded
the digital yuan app.

00:02:04.103 --> 00:02:08.020
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:10.410
- [Narrator] It recorded
that he spent money

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.640
on lunch and medicine
one Saturday afternoon

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.131
in the southwestern city of Chengdu.

00:02:15.131 --> 00:02:19.048
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:23.110
- [Narrator] About 10,000
merchants in Chengdu

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:25.820
have signed up to accept digital yuan.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:26.980
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.560
- [Narrator] Zhong Jiaying
manages a dumpling restaurant

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.040
and she said the digital yuan

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.246
has some advantages compared
with other payment options.

00:02:34.246 --> 00:02:38.163
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:41.640
- [Narrator] For instance, two of China's

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.824
most popular digital wallets
charge merchants an average

00:02:44.824 --> 00:02:47.770
of .6% for every transaction.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.930
There's also another upside in the works.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.050
The central bank is planning

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:52.520
to make transactions possible

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.720
even without an internet connection.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.790
So restaurants like
Zhong's won't have to worry

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.080
about their spotty connections

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:01.630
that sometimes make it hard to
process digital transactions.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:05.010
- This digital yuan is less about money

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.600
and more about data.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.760
- [Narrator] Yaya Fanusie
is an adjunct senior fellow

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:10.230
at the nonprofit think tank

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.260
Center for a New American Security

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:13.730
in Washington, D.C.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.440
He's been studying digital currencies

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.920
for the past six years

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.620
and he says China's new currency

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.780
is not as anonymous as it claims.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:21.680
- The central bank has talked

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.680
about there being controllable anonymity,

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.330
which really means it's
anonymous horizontally, right?

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.790
The users that are using
it don't necessarily know

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:32.050
the identity of everyone
that they're interaction with

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:34.420
but vertically, it's not anonymous.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:35.950
The central bank is at the top

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.140
with information on all the users.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:39.660
- [Narrator] China's
central bank has promised

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.480
to protect users' privacy.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.470
For now, people can
choose whether they want

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.400
to use the digital currency.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:46.710
But the central bank has said

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:49.350
that as the country
becomes a cashless society,

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:52.080
it expects the digital yuan
to become the primary way

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.490
to make transactions.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:57.184
- The Chinese government
could force Chinese companies

00:03:57.184 --> 00:04:00.860
to only accept payment in digital yuan,

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.510
which would then force
the foreign companies,

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.130
their foreign counterparts for trade.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:06.910
It could ensure that
they have to use that.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:08.230
- [Narrator] Central banks have authority

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:09.650
to control money supply

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:12.000
but their actions to
restrict a digital currency

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.790
would have a more immediate effect,

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.610
leaving companies holding that currency

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.330
all the more vulnerable.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.900
For example, Fanusie
says China's central bank

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:22.546
have put an expiration
date on the digital money,

00:04:22.546 --> 00:04:25.220
similar to how lottery
winnings have to be spent

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.490
before a certain date.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.050
- It means that the Chinese government

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.417
could set up a whole lot of things

00:04:29.417 --> 00:04:32.840
to have your currency maybe valid

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.130
or invalid based on its own priorities.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.490
This is almost like handing over the keys

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:41.130
to your business or to
your finance department

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:41.963
in some ways

00:04:41.963 --> 00:04:44.280
because you really can't control what,

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.230
at the end of the day,

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:48.604
may happen with the funds
that you're holding.

00:04:48.604 --> 00:04:50.080
- [Narrator] While there
are privacy concerns,

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.810
Fanusie says digital currencies

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.310
can create more efficient monetary policy

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:56.260
and counter criminal activities.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.930
China's central bank said
its digital yuan system

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.610
would help combat money laundering,

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:02.948
gambling and terrorism financing.

00:05:02.948 --> 00:05:06.410
(speaking in foreign language)

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.300
Meanwhile, the central
bank is also looking

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.950
into ways to make international
transactions possible

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.389
in digital yuan.

00:05:12.389 --> 00:05:14.330
And Fanusie says there's a big variable

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.610
that'll determine if that's going to work.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:19.150
- Will foreign governments
allow their businesses

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:23.000
and citizens to hold
digital yuan and use it?

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.490
It's not a given that all other countries

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:27.350
are going to transact with this

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:31.040
and because of the
privacy, the data issues.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.863
So this is really to be determined.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:36.690
- [Narrator] While there's no set date

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.130
for a national rollout,

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:40.250
some officials have said
the digital currency

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.550
could be ready for wider use next February

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:45.110
during the 2022 Winter
Olympics in Beijing.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:48.007
- I think there is an
element of showing off

00:05:48.007 --> 00:05:51.500
for the big international audience.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.360
We have a central bank digital currency

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:54.340
that we're using.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:57.220
We're the biggest country that's doing it.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:59.610
- [Narrator] And China isn't
alone in this experiment.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.870
According to one survey of central banks,

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:04.250
86% of them from the US to Japan

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:06.760
are exploring these types of currencies.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.040
For early digital yuan winners like Huang,

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:10.611
he says the trial went smoothly

00:06:10.611 --> 00:06:12.838
and if the currency does go mainstream,

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:16.542
he expects the surveillance
aspect will matter less to him.

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:20.459
(speaking in foreign language)

00:06:31.215 --> 00:06:33.798
(lively music)

